meta {
  name: Get Access
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/daily-reports/access
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    console.log(`✅ Today (IST): ${res.body.today} | team tab: ${res.body.canViewTeam} | scope: ${res.body.scope} | employees: ${res.body.teamSize}`);
  } else {
    console.log("❌", res.body.error);
  }
}

docs {
  # Get Access

  What the logged-in user can see on the Daily Report page. Any logged-in user
  (Requestor, Intern, RM, HOD, …).

  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "today": "2026-11-23",
    "backdateLimitDays": 0,
    "canViewTeam": true,
    "scope": "team",
    "teamSize": 6,
    "depts": []
  }
  ```

  - `today` — current date in IST (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
  - `backdateLimitDays` — `0` = same-day only (default). Set by env `DAILY_REPORT_BACKDATE_DAYS`.
  - `canViewTeam` — show the **Team Reports** tab: the user is the **HOD** of at least one
    employee, or is SuperUser / Admin.
  - `scope` — `"team"` (employees whose HOD is this user) or `"all"` (SuperUser, Admin).
  - `teamSize` — number of employees the user can see.
  - `depts` — department filter list (only filled for `scope: "all"`).

  ## Who sees an employee's daily reports
  Only the employee's own **HOD**, **SuperUser** and **Admin** — view only.
  RM, Management and HR DeptHOD do not see them. There is **no approve / return** step.
}
